object_literal_this_errors.velt:31:14: error: `this` in an object-literal method is supported only where the literal implements an interface or has no expected type
  = note: TypeScript allows this (`this` is the object the method is called on); here the method is stored as a plain function, which has no object to use as `this`
  = note: declare the expected type as an interface (`interface T { m(): R }`), or use the object's variable instead of `this`

object_literal_this_errors.velt:39:14: error: `this` in an object-literal method is supported only where the literal implements an interface or has no expected type
  = note: TypeScript allows this (`this` is the object the method is called on); here the method is stored as a plain function, which has no object to use as `this`
  = note: declare the expected type as an interface (`interface T { m(): R }`), or use the object's variable instead of `this`

object_literal_this_errors.velt:46:5: error: the result type of method `loop` cannot be inferred: it depends on its own result through `this`
  = note: write it: `loop(): T`

object_literal_this_errors.velt:54:9: error: parameter `k` of method `add` needs a type: the object literal has no expected type
  = note: write its type, or annotate the literal with an interface that declares the method

object_literal_this_errors.velt:66:20: error: the method `get` uses `this`, so it cannot be read as a value
  = note: TypeScript allows this, but `this` is then the object the function is called on, if any (`undefined` for a plain call, which throws a TypeError in strict mode)
  = note: call the method on its object, or wrap the call in an arrow function: `(...) => o.get(...)`

object_literal_this_errors.velt:67:29: error: the method `get` uses `this`, so it cannot be read as a value
  = note: TypeScript allows this, but `this` is then the object the function is called on, if any (`undefined` for a plain call, which throws a TypeError in strict mode)
  = note: call the method on its object, or wrap the call in an arrow function: `(...) => o.get(...)`

object_literal_this_errors.velt:89:19: error: `C.s` uses `this` or `super`, so it cannot be used as a value
  = note: a static method taken as a value has no `this` (JavaScript calls it with `this` undefined)
  = note: call it as `C.s()`, or wrap the call: `() => C.s()`

object_literal_this_errors.velt:72:31: error: the value of property `m` is a function not written in the literal, and a method named `m` may use `this`, so it is not supported yet
  = note: Node calls it with the literal as `this` (`o.m()`), while Velt keeps the object a method read as a value was read from
  = note: write the function in the literal: `m: (...args) => c.m(...args)`, or a method `m(...) { ... }`

